==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*5 [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 4~5.33 seconds<sup>120f~160f</sup>.
*5 [[Zigge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 4~5.33 seconds<sup>120f~160f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**8 [[Those Guys]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**3 [[Hippoe]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 4~5.33 seconds<sup>120f~160f</sup>.
**3 [[Pigge]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 4~5.33 seconds<sup>120f~160f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The base's HP isn't a lot, considering how many enemies burrow. Get as many units behind the [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] as possible, then stall for time until the units that slipped by destroy the base. For units, try to use fast attackers, like [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]] or [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Rocker Cat]]. A zombie killer like [[Piledriver Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Piledriver Cat]] might be useful too.

